# design docs (keep screenshots for README). Pre-build planning notes — wireframes,
# MVP scope, stack bake-offs — stay local: they described intentions, and the code is
# now the truth. The exceptions are the ones another tracked file tells you to read:
# docs/TESTING.md (linked from CONTRIBUTING.md) documents how to run the suite, and
# docs/API_CHANGES.md (linked from RELEASING.md) carries breaking API changes into the
# next release's notes — a release process that depends on an untracked file is one that
# silently stops working for everyone but its author.
docs/*.md
!docs/TESTING.md
!docs/API_CHANGES.md
docs/*.txt

# Local Claude context
CLAUDE.md
.claude/

# Playwright artifacts
web/e2e/.auth/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
.playwright-mcp/

# Local Fable/Sonnet porting specs (working artifacts, not committed)
.workouts-port/

# Built mobile APKs — pulled from EAS for local testing, ~107MB each. Releases are
# distributed as GitHub release assets, never committed.
/releases/

# Ad-hoc screenshots dropped at the repo root during local testing. Scoped to the
# root only — mobile/assets, web/public and README screenshots stay tracked.
/*.png

# Design-system export (fonts, ui_kits, raw asset dumps) — local working material.
/design/

# MCP server config: machine-specific absolute paths, not portable across checkouts.
.mcp.json

# Maestro flows are local-only dev artifacts, same call as 5fc269a ("remove stray
# Maestro flow committed with #61"). Nothing in CI runs them — they need a device and
# a running backend — so a committed flow is a file that rots without anyone noticing.
# The rule exists because the convention alone did not hold: without it the same mistake
# landed twice, and the second time it reached main.
mobile/.maestro/

# Vite writes these when a dev server exits hard
web/vite.config.ts.timestamp-*
